// SB+fence.
//
// Store buffering with a fence after one of the two stores only; the other
//   store can still be buffered.
//
// Asserted below, by source:
//   herd7 on the zoo's cat models, run on this program: TSO allows, Coherence
//     allows.
//   the zoo's equivalence and ordering edges:
//     SC forbids. SC forbids SB, and a fence adds no behaviour.
//     VbD forbids. Equivalent to SC (zoo edge).
//     x86-TSO allows. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     ClightTSO allows. Equivalent to x86-TSO (zoo edge).
//   Not asserted, for want of a verdict to check against: RC11, RC11z, RC17,
//     OD-LSO, MRD, CC, PC, PRAM, Causal, Slow, Local, POCausal, RYW, MR, MW,
//     WFR. RA, SRA and WRA are defined on release stores and acquire loads, and
//     this program has other accesses.
x := 0; y := 0;
{
  x := 1;
  fence(sc);
  r0 := y
} ||| {
  y := 1;
  r1 := x
}
%%
allow (r0 = 0 && r1 = 0) [TSO, x86-TSO, ClightTSO, Coherence]
forbid (r0 = 0 && r1 = 0) [SC, VbD]
